    "created_at": "2020-12-29T20:06:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-12-29T20:06:47Z",
    "body": "This is an interesting idea. Rather than adding permission revocation to WebHID API I think it would be better to allow WebHID permissions to be revoked through the [Permissions API](https://www.w3.org/TR/permissions/).\r\n\r\nIn Chrome it's already possible for users to revoke WebHID device permissions in the Site Information popup. Click the lock icon next to the address bar, then click the X icon next to devices that you want to revoke. You can do the same thing in Site Settings (chrome://settings/content/hidDevices). However there's no way to revoke permissions by script.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
